@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   This project's root namespace is ExSheet.MudBlazor, so a plain "MudBlazor" here is this
   namespace, not MudBlazor's, and every product using is written with global:: (the name
   collisions in AGENTS.md). *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::MudBlazor
@using global::ExSheet
@* Not the contract (ADR-0201): MudSheetChrome draws a Sheet Tab's menu with this, and no Consumer
   places it. It is public only because Razor makes every component public, is hidden from a
   Consumer's editor, and may change in any version. *@
@attribute [System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsable(System.ComponentModel.EditorBrowsableState.Never)]
@*
    A Sheet Tab's menu as the MudBlazor Chrome draws it (ADR-0331 §4; exsheet-workbook ticket 06): a
    MudPaper holding each command with its MudIcon and its name in MudText, the active one marked in the
    palette's primary. ExSheet keeps the element around it, which holds the keyboard and answers the
    menu's keys, so nothing here takes DOM focus: a command is a plain element that names itself for
    aria-activedescendant and calls back into the context when clicked. It is not a MudMenu, whose list
    MudBlazor draws in its popover provider, outside the Sheet, where a click is not in the Sheet's Input
    Order (ADR-0240 section 6), and whose own keys would hand the keyboard to its button. No script is
    added (ADR-0021).
*@
<MudPaper Elevation="8" Class="mud-ex-sheet-tab-menu">
    @foreach (var command in Context.Commands)
    {
        <div id="@command.Id" role="menuitem" aria-disabled="@(command.Enabled ? null : "true")" title="@command.DisabledReason"
             class="@ItemClass(command)" @onclick="command.Invoke">
            <MudIcon Icon="@IconOf(command.Kind)" Size="Size.Small" Color="@(command.Active ? Color.Primary : Color.Default)" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" HtmlTag="span">@command.Label</MudText>
        </div>
    }
</MudPaper>

@code {
    /// <summary>The menu ExSheet describes.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public SheetTabMenuContext Context { get; set; } = default!;

    private static string ItemClass(SheetTabCommand command) =>
        "mud-ex-sheet-tab-command" + (command.Active ? " mud-ex-sheet-tab-command-active" : "")
        + (command.Enabled ? "" : " mud-ex-sheet-tab-command-disabled");

    private static string IconOf(SheetTabCommandKind kind) => kind switch
    {
        SheetTabCommandKind.Rename => Icons.Material.Filled.DriveFileRenameOutline,
        SheetTabCommandKind.Delete => Icons.Material.Filled.Delete,
        SheetTabCommandKind.MoveLeft => Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronLeft,
        SheetTabCommandKind.MoveRight => Icons.Material.Filled.ChevronRight,
        _ => Icons.Material.Filled.ContentCopy,
    };
}
